          "is_highlight": false
        },
        {
          "title": "The Chameleon's Limit: Investigating Persona Collapse and Homogenization in Large Language Models",
          "title_zh": "变色龙的极限：探究大语言模型中的角色坍缩与同质化",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2604.24698v2",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2604.24698",
          "summary": "The paper formalizes Persona Collapse, where LLM agents given detailed human profiles cluster into a few response classes rather than covering population diversity, and quantifies it with coverage, uniformity and complexity metrics. Across eight LLMs on personality, moral reasoning and self-introduction tasks, collapse was universal but task-dependent, sampling more personas did not mitigate it, and persona-targeted fine-tuning narrowed the population further.",
          "keywords": [
            {
